@startuml poll-review
' cumin works - the Reviewer request (I3), the check of its review after the run, the kept step after a temporary failure, I5, I8, and I10.
' Document: poll.md, section on the Reviewer request.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:I3: every required check passed on the head commit;
:Read the login of the Reviewer App
and the last cumin/status/ready of the issue;
:Count the round from the reviews on GitHub
(pure function);
:Change the label to cumin/status/reviewing;
:Remove the Reviewer worktree,
open the head commit detached;
if (Round?) then (1)
  :New session;
else (2 or later)
  :Resume the Reviewer session;
  :Name the last reviewed commit;
endif
if (The Reviewer approved an earlier commit?) then (yes)
  :Name the last approved commit
  (round 1: review only the diff from it);
else (no)
endif
repeat
  :Run the Reviewer ("review");
  if (Result?) then (blocked)
    repeat
      :I10: read the issue of the run again;
      backward :Keep the step (in memory).
      The issue stays in work, with its label.
      A poll 5 minutes later runs it again;
    repeat while (The read failed with
    a temporary failure?) is (yes) not (no)
    :Hand back to the Owner
    (blocked_reason, no retry);
    stop
  elseif (abnormal end) then
    :Retry once in a new session,
    then hand back to the Owner (row I3);
    stop
  else (done)
    repeat
      :Read the issue of the run again;
      backward :Keep the step (in memory).
      The issue stays in work, with its label.
      A poll 5 minutes later runs it again;
    repeat while (A call to GitHub of this step failed
    with a temporary failure? (this read, or below:
    the required checks, a label change)) is (yes) not (no)
  endif
  backward:Ask once more in the same session;
repeat while (Latest review of the Reviewer is on the head
commit with APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES?) is (no, first time)
->yes, or no for the second time;
if (Review?) then (APPROVE)
  :Log it; the label stays
  (the merge is a later requirement);
elseif (REQUEST_CHANGES) then
  if (Round below max_review_rounds?) then (yes)
    :I5: change the label to cumin/status/implementing;
    :Ask the Implementer to fix the comments
    (its own session, the branch of the pull request);
    :I2, the checks, and I3 again;
  else (no)
    :I8: ask the Reviewer to explain the cause
    (the same session);
    if (A decision request of the Reviewer
    after its last review?) then (yes)
      :Change the label to cumin/status/awaiting-decision;
      :Notify the Owner (link: that comment);
    else (no, or blocked, or abnormal twice)
      :Hand back to the Owner (row I8);
    endif
  endif
else (none, twice)
  :Hand back to the Owner (row I5);
endif
stop
@enduml
